dit/080: ggml-opencl gives the GPU back to the screen. The S25 lagged severely running Z-Image on OpenCL with 2.2 GB
of RAM free: the UI and the DiT share the Adreno, and single dispatches ran 40-85 ms (an FFN matmul, all 30 heads of
attention) against a frame's 8-16 ms. All off unless set:
  GGML_OPENCL_YIELD_EVERY=N     wait for the queue every N ops, then sleep GGML_OPENCL_YIELD_US (2000)
  GGML_OPENCL_MM_MAX_GFLOP=G    a matmul in token chunks of at most G GFLOP (exact: views, sums unchanged)
  GGML_OPENCL_FA_SPLIT_HEADS=H  attention H heads per dispatch (views; whole GQA groups)
  GGML_OPENCL_FA_SPLIT_Q=R      attention R query rows per dispatch (views; exact, each row on its own)
  GGML_OPENCL_YIELD_LOG=1       each graph's longest wait, with the op and its shapes
